<article class="env-lemma" id="0DPX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DPX">Lemma <span data-tag="0DPX">108.12.2</span>.</a> The morphism $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{omplexes}_{X/B} \to B$ is quasi-separated and locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To check $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{omplexes}_{X/B} \to B$ is quasi-separated we have to show that its diagonal is quasi-compact and quasi-separated. This is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/0DPW" data-tag="0DPW">108.12.1</a>. To prove that $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{omplexes}_{X/B} \to B$ is locally of finite presentation, we have to show that $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{omplexes}_{X/B} \to B$ is limit preserving, see Limits of Stacks, Proposition <a href="/tag/0CMY" data-tag="0CMY">102.3.8</a>. This follows from Quot, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DLJ" data-tag="0DLJ">99.16.8</a> (small detail omitted). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>